# standard25.env -- the ISPD 2025 one-route setting (2026-10-14, HISTORY_COST_SWEEP.md Part 133). Since
# 2026-10-16 the 2025 standard flow is gr/timing_loop.py (Part 134), which scores candidate routes with
# the contest's OpenROAD; this file is the fallback where OpenROAD is not available. Layered on the 2024
# standard:
#   ./pd39route @standard.env @standard24.env @fast24.env @standard25.env <design>.cap <design>.net <out>
# Timing plus capacitance: nets whose input pin slack is negative fall in three classes (slack /
# the design's worst >= 0.1, 0.4, 0.7) and pay resistance-weighted wirelength (k per class); every
# net also pays capacitance-weighted wirelength (kp). Both strengths are scaled by the design's own
# score weights (PD39ROUTE_TIMING_SCALE=weights: timing by |w_TNS| / w_overflow x |worst slack|,
# power by w_power / w_overflow, each relative to ariane's). Measured against our own unbiased
# routes (score change, lower is better): ariane -2.16, bsg_chip -1.38, NV_NVDLA_partition_c -6.22,
# mempool_tile_wrap -0.51; ariane's score 2.30 -> ~0.14 (1st place 0.90).
# R and C per layer (metal1..metal10) are NanGate45's, from the contest's setRC.tcl -- every 2025
# design uses that stack; another technology needs its own values.
PD37ROUTE_THREADS=8
PD39ROUTE_TIMING_LAYERS=40,80,160
PD39ROUTE_POWER_LAYERS=4
PD39ROUTE_TIMING_SCALE=weights
PD39ROUTE_LAYER_R=5.4286e-03,3.5714e-03,3.5714e-03,1.5e-03,1.5e-03,1.5e-03,1.875e-04,1.875e-04,3.75e-05,3.75e-05
PD39ROUTE_LAYER_C=7.41819e-02,6.74606e-02,8.88758e-02,1.07121e-01,1.08964e-01,1.02044e-01,1.10436e-01,9.69714e-02,3.6864e-02,2.8042e-02
